; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Trap.c	   203  /*! \brief          Returns whether access to certain privileges requires a trap.
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Trap.c	   204   *  \details        Used when it is partly known whether certain privileges are required.
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Trap.c	   205   *                  - If the ThreadPointer is readable in user mode, known information can be used
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Trap.c	   206   *                  - Otherwise, decision is made based on current privileges if possible
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Trap.c	   207   *
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Trap.c	   208   *  \param[in]      IsTrapRequired  Defines whether supervisor mode is required to access required privileges:
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Trap.c	   209   *                                   - TRUE:  Trap shall be forced even if the thread pointer can be read in user mode
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Trap.c	   210   *                                            (unless supervisor mode is already active).
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Trap.c	   211   *                                   - FALSE: Trap shall be performed, if system state (i.e. ThreadPointer) can only be
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Trap.c	   212   *                                            read after a trap.
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Trap.c	   213   *
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Trap.c	   214   *  \retval         !0  A trap is required to access the ThreadPointer or other privileges.
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Trap.c	   215   *  \retval         0   No trap is required, the ThreadPointer can be accessed directly and no additional privileges
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Trap.c	   216   *                      are needed.
